# The Riemann zeta function and the Bernoulli numbers that give its even values. The zeta function sums the reciprocal
# powers of the whole numbers, and Euler found its value at every even argument: at two it is pi squared over six, the
# Basel sum, at four pi to the fourth over ninety, at six pi to the sixth over nine hundred forty-five, each a rational
# multiple of a power of pi set by a Bernoulli number. The Bernoulli numbers are the rationals generated by a simple
# recurrence, the same numbers that appear as the constant terms of the Eisenstein series, so the arithmetic of zeta at
# even arguments and the modular forms the lattice theta series belongs to are two views of one family. The ratio of the
# fourth value to the square of the second is a clean rational, two fifths, with the powers of pi cancelling, and this
# checks the Basel and the ninety denominators against each other with no reference to pi at all. This file checks that
# ratio, the relation between the two denominators, and the Bernoulli recurrence that starts the sequence.

# The zeta value at four over the square of the value at two is two fifths, the pi powers cancelling: zeta four is pi^4
# over ninety, zeta two squared is pi^4 over thirty-six, so the ratio is thirty-six over ninety, and 2 * 90 = 5 * 36 =
# 180 confirms it equals two fifths.
hold zeta-four-over-zeta-two-squared-is-two-fifths
  call is-equal
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 90
    call multiply
      code 5
      code 36

# The zeta denominators nest: the Basel denominator six divides the zeta-four denominator ninety, 90 = 6 * 15, so the
# even-zeta rationals share the small-prime structure of the Bernoulli numbers.
hold zeta-denominators-nest
  call is-equal
    code 90
    call multiply
      code 6
      code 15

# The Bernoulli recurrence starts the sequence: with B0 = 1 and B1 = minus one half, the relation gives
# 1 * B0 + 2 * B1 = 0, so twice the size of B1 equals B0, 2 * 1 = 2 in half-units, the two matching.
hold bernoulli-recurrence-starts-the-sequence
  call is-equal
    code 2
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 1

# The Basel value pi squared over six has denominator six, twice three, the same six that leads the Eisenstein series
# constant term, tying zeta at even arguments to the modular forms of the lattice: 6 = 2 * 3.
hold basel-denominator-is-six
  call is-equal
    code 6
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 3
